Okay, we have placeholders for a lot of stuff, but I think it makes sense to
get real nav data & real plates & complete charts in place to do further
adventuring.  We have the fixture doing a lot of work that should be getting
done by a real data stream. Some of the things:
- We should probably be pulling the aviation database from runs/20260407T053200Z-data-build/work/data/databases.zip
- We should activate all four chart tile sources for all areas: Sectional, TAC, IFR Low, IFR High
	- the old avare app "uses hardcoded chart-type lists and hardcoded coverage polygons";
	we should replace that with a metadata index file
- We should index and make accessible all the TPP/CSUP data. Again, the avare app just used
the filesystem contents for that index. We might want to construct a metadata index file
that travels with the top-level database.zip, so that the UI can tell you what you're
missing (for example).

